#N Gosper glider gun
#C The first known finite pattern with unbounded growth, found by Bill Gosper
#C in 1970. It emits one glider every 30 generations, so the population grows
#C without bound while the gun itself returns to its starting shape.
#C
#C Placed near the centre of the 2^64 x 2^64 universe. The origin and
#C generation lines below are this project's extension for restoring absolute
#C position in a universe far larger than RLE was designed to describe; they
#C are plain #C comments, so any standard Life tool ignores them and reads
#C this as an ordinary glider gun.
#C origin: 9223372036854775790 9223372036854775804
